#: INSTRUCTIONS1.md:1
msgid "PLUMED Masterclass 21.6: Dimensionality reduction"
msgstr "PLUMED Masterclass 21.6：Dimensionality Reduction"

#: INSTRUCTIONS1.md:3
msgid "Aims"
msgstr "目的"

#: INSTRUCTIONS1.md:5
msgid ""
"The primary aim of this Masterclass is to show you how you might use PLUMED "
"in your work. We will see how to call PLUMED from a python notebook and "
"discuss some strategies for selecting collective variables."
msgstr ""
"この Masterclass の主な目的は、自身の研究で PLUMED をどのように活用できるかを示すことである。Python Notebook から "
"PLUMED を呼び出す方法を学び、Collective Variables を選ぶための戦略を検討する。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS1.md:9
msgid "Objectives"
msgstr "到達目標"

#: INSTRUCTIONS1.md:11
msgid "Once this section is completed, users will be able to:"
msgstr "この節を終えると、次ができます。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS1.md:13
msgid "Calculate CVs and import them into a python notebook."
msgstr "CV を計算し Python Notebook に取り込む。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS1.md:14
msgid "Generate visualizations of data using chemiscope"
msgstr "Chemiscope で可視化する。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS1.md:16
msgid "Acknowledgements"
msgstr "謝辞"

#: INSTRUCTIONS1.md:18
msgid ""
"Throughout this exercise, we use the [atomistic simulation "
"environment](https://wiki.fysik.dtu.dk/ase/) and "
"[chemiscope](https://chemiscope.org/). Please look at the information at the"
" links I have provided here for more information about these codes."
msgstr ""
"この演習では [atomistic simulation environment](https://wiki.fysik.dtu.dk/ase/) と "
"[chemiscope](https://chemiscope.org/) を用いる。これらのコードの詳細は、各リンク先の情報を参照してほしい。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS1.md:22
msgid "Setting up the software"
msgstr "ソフトウェアのセットアップ"

#: INSTRUCTIONS1.md:24
msgid ""
"For this Masterclass, you will need to set up the plumed and gromacs as you "
"did for [this masterclass](https://www.plumed.org/doc-v2.8/user-"
"doc/html/masterclass-21-1.html). You thus install plumed and gromacs using:"
msgstr ""
"[この Masterclass](https://www.plumed.org/doc-v2.8/user-"
"doc/html/masterclass-21-1.html) と同様に PLUMED・GROMACS を設定します。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS1.md:31
msgid "You can install the other software you need using:"
msgstr "ほかのソフトウェアは次で入れます。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS1.md:37
msgid ""
"Notice that you need a package called ase (the atomic simulation "
"environment) for these exercises and the other packages you have been using."
" You also need to install chemiscope, which you can do by using the "
"following command:"
msgstr ""
"従来の Package に加え ASE (Atomic Simulation Environment) と Chemiscope "
"が必要です。後者は次で入れます。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS1.md:44
msgid "Resources"
msgstr "資料"

#: INSTRUCTIONS1.md:46
msgid ""
"The data needed to complete this Masterclass can be found on "
"[GitHub](https://github.com/plumed/masterclass-21-6). You can clone this "
"repository locally on your machine using the following command:"
msgstr ""
"この Masterclass に必要なデータは [GitHub](https://github.com/plumed/masterclass-21-6)"
" にある。次のコマンドで、このリポジトリを自分のマシンに clone できる。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS1.md:53
msgid ""
"I recommend that you run each exercise in a separate sub-directory (i.e. "
"Exercise-1, Exercise-2, ...), which you can create inside the root directory"
" `masterclass-21-6`. Organizing your data this way will help you to keep "
"things clean."
msgstr ""
"各演習は、`masterclass-21-6` "
"のルートディレクトリ内に作成した個別のサブディレクトリ（Exercise-1、Exercise-2、…）で実行することを推奨する。このように整理すると、データを管理しやすくなる。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS1.md:55
msgid "_All the exercises have been tested with PLUMED version 2.7.0._"
msgstr "_すべての演習は PLUMED 2.7.0 で動作確認されている。_"

#: INSTRUCTIONS1.md:57
msgid "Exercises"
msgstr "演習"

#: INSTRUCTIONS1.md:59
msgid "Exercise 1: Running PLUMED from a python notebook"
msgstr "演習1：Python Notebook から PLUMED を実行"

#: INSTRUCTIONS1.md:61
msgid ""
"I like working with Python notebooks. Using notebooks allows me to keep the "
"codes that I am working on close to the explanations of how these codes "
"work. I can also make all my figures within a notebook. By using notebooks, "
"I can thus have a single file that contains:"
msgstr "私は Notebook を好んで使います。コードの近くに説明を置き、図も同じ場所で作れるので、1ファイルに次をまとめられます。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS1.md:64
msgid "Discussion of the work done."
msgstr "行った作業の議論。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS1.md:65
msgid "The analysis code."
msgstr "解析コード。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS1.md:66
msgid "The final figures that were generated."
msgstr "最終的な図。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS1.md:68
msgid ""
"In previous masterclasses we have run plumed driver through bash from within"
" a notebook by using commands like the one shown below:"
msgstr "これまでは Notebook 内の Bash で driver を次のように実行しました。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS1.md:76
msgid ""
"We have then read in the colvar file produced and analyzed it from within "
"the notebook. We can avoid using plumed driver and can call plumed directly "
"from python using the python interface. The code below, for instance, "
"generates the plot underneath the code. The code reads in the trajectory "
"from the file traj.pdb that you obtained from the GitHub repository. The "
"plot then shows how the $\\phi$ angle on the second residue of the protein "
"changes with time."
msgstr ""
"その後 COLVAR を読んで解析しましたが、Python Interface で直接呼ぶこともできます。次は GitHub の traj.pdb "
"を読み、残基2の $\\phi$ の時間変化を描きます。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS1.md:142
msgid ""
"![The value of the phi angle as a function of "
"time.](figures/masterclass-21-6-phi-time.png)"
msgstr "![phi 角の時間変化](figures/masterclass-21-6-phi-time.png)"

#: INSTRUCTIONS1.md:144
msgid ""
"__Your task in this first exercise is to modify the code above and to "
"produce a figure similar to the one shown below.__ This figure shows all the"
" values of the $\\phi$ and $\\psi$ angles in the second residue of the "
"protein during the simulation."
msgstr "__上のコードを変え、次の図を作ってください。__ 残基2の $\\phi$ と $\\psi$ の全値を示します。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS1.md:147
msgid ""
"![A plot showing phi against psi for the second residue of the "
"protein.](figures/masterclass-21-6-phi-psi.png)"
msgstr "![残基2の phi と psi](figures/masterclass-21-6-phi-psi.png)"

#: INSTRUCTIONS1.md:149
msgid "Exercise 2: Generating a chemiscope representation"
msgstr "演習2：Chemiscope 表示の生成"

#: INSTRUCTIONS1.md:151
msgid ""
"Plots showing the trajectory in CV space similar to those you generated at "
"the end of the previous exercise are helpful. What would be more useful, "
"however, is some way of understanding the relationship between the positions"
" in CV space and the structures of the various atoms. In other words, what "
"we would like is something like this:"
msgstr "CV 空間の図は有用ですが、位置と原子構造の関係を知りたいものです。次のような表示を目指します。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS1.md:155
msgid ""
"![A representation of the time against phi plot from the previous exercise "
"that was generated using "
"chemiscope.](figures/masterclass-21-6-chemiscope.png)"
msgstr ""
"![Chemiscope による前の時間対 phi の図](figures/masterclass-21-6-chemiscope.png)"

#: INSTRUCTIONS1.md:157
msgid ""
"You can see the frame in the trajectory that each point in the plot "
"corresponds to from the above figure. The snapshots on the right correspond "
"to the structures the system had at the points highlighted in red, yellow, "
"green and blue respectively in the plot on the left."
msgstr "各点の Trajectory Frame がわかります。右の Snapshot は左の赤・黄・緑・青の点に対応します。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS1.md:160
msgid ""
"The figure above was generated using chemiscope. This server allows you to "
"generate and interact with plots like the one shown above. __Your task in "
"this exercise is to generate your own chemiscope representation of the data "
"in traj.pdb.__ To create a chemiscope representation of the $\\phi$ angles "
"that we generated using the first python script from the previous exercise, "
"you would add the following python code:"
msgstr ""
"Chemiscope ではこのような図を作り操作できます。__traj.pdb を自分で表示してください。__ 前の最初の Python の "
"$\\phi$ を使うには、次を加えます。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS1.md:199
msgid ""
"You would then upload the `torsion_chemiscope.json.gz` file that is "
"generated by this script at "
"[https://chemiscope.org](https://chemiscope.org)."
msgstr ""
"生成した `torsion_chemiscope.json.gz` を "
"[https://chemiscope.org](https://chemiscope.org) に Upload します。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS1.md:201
msgid ""
"__See if you can generate your own chemiscope representation of the data in "
"traj.pdb.__ I would recommend calculating and uploading a chemiscope "
"representation of all the protein's torsional angles. At the very least, you"
" need to do at least two backbone torsional angles. However, if you do more "
"than two torsions, you can generate a plot like the one shown below."
msgstr ""
"__traj.pdb を自分で表示してください。__ 全 Torsion Angle の計算・Upload を推奨します。最低2つの Backbone "
"Torsion が必要ですが、増やすと次の図も作れます。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS1.md:203
msgid ""
"![\"A representation of the trajectory that was generated using chemiscope. "
"Here psi_2 is plotted on the x-axis, phi_2 is plotted on the y-axis, and "
"phi_3 is plotted on the z-axis. The points are coloured following the value "
"of psi_3, and the points' sizes are proportional to "
"phi_4.\"](figures/masterclass-21-6-chemiscope2.png)"
msgstr ""
"![Chemiscope 表示。x は psi_2、y は phi_2、z は phi_3、色は psi_3、点の大きさは "
"phi_4](figures/masterclass-21-6-chemiscope2.png)"

#: INSTRUCTIONS1.md:205
msgid "Summary"
msgstr "まとめ"

#: INSTRUCTIONS1.md:207
msgid ""
"You can do your analsysis by running PLUMED from python directly. Similarly "
"you can hopefully think of ways to use chemiscope to visualise your own "
"trajectories. We will use these techniques in the exercises that follow but "
"hopefully you can already see that they will be useful for your own "
"research."
msgstr ""
"Python から直接 PLUMED を解析に使い、Chemiscope を自分の Trajectory "
"にも応用できます。以後の演習でも使いますが、自分の研究にも役立つはずです。"
